The following scoped exceptions take precedence over that default:

* The primary Xbox port's imported and adapted GPLv2 source remains
  GPL-2.0-only. In particular, xbox/third_party/castlevania-cod-pc is governed
  by its own LICENSE and README, and xbox/tools/imported_game_state.py and
  xbox/tools/imported_game_profiles.json retain the donor's GPLv2 terms.
  The donor's sdk-patches/ is an explicit MIT exception made by its author;
  preserve its copyright and MIT terms. This default does not relicense any
  upstream code or grant a GPLv3 option for the GPLv2-only donor.
* The experimental PS2 host in src/, PS2-specific runtime patches in patches/,
  and modifications derived from PS2Recomp or PCSX2 are GPL-3.0-or-later for
  project-authored contributions. Upstream terms and more specific notices
  still apply. No GPLv2 option is granted for GPLv3-derived material.
* Original Noble Archimedes branding art, icons, and synthetic audio in
  assets/noble/ are dedicated under CC0-1.0 to the extent the contributors
  hold rights in them. Source generators remain under the code default
  unless explicitly marked otherwise. Game-derived content and third-party
  assets are excluded from this dedication.
* Submodules, vendor/third_party trees, external dependencies and copied or
  adapted upstream code retain their own licenses and copyright notices,
  wherever located. This includes tools/PS2Recomp, tools/xboxrecomp,
  tools/rea, Xbox runtime copies and the borrowed Halo renderer material
  in xbox/src/d3d8gl/. File-level notices override the project default.

